# Patterns here are gitignore-style and are matched against the whole cloned
# repository, not just this directory — an unanchored `media/` also matches
# frontend/app/api/media/, which it must not. Both spellings are listed because
# the base the patterns resolve against differs with the project's Root
# Directory setting; each is exact, so a stray match isn't possible either way.

# Uploaded media is user data on the VPS deployment. It has no meaning on
# Vercel — the filesystem is read-only there — and uploading it would only make
# every deploy slower.
/media/
backend/media/

# Built by Vercel, never shipped to it.
/dist/
backend/dist/

# Secrets belong in the project's environment variables, never in the bundle.
# Left unanchored on purpose: an .env at any depth should stay out.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
